{
  "slug": "trunk",
  "name": "Trunk",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Flaky test detection, root cause analysis, and fix suggestions for development teams. Connects to the Trunk MCP server to analyze flaky tests in your CI pipeline, explain why they're flaky, and suggest targeted fixes.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **2 skills**, **3 commands** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (2): `flaky-test-patterns` (Common flaky test patterns and how to fix them), `trunk-ci-setup` (Best practices for configuring CI pipelines to upload test results to Trunk)\n- **Commands** (3): `fix-flaky` (Get root cause analysis and apply a fix for a flaky test), `setup-uploads` (Set up test result uploads to Trunk for your repository), `why-flaky` (Explain why a test is flaky without applying changes)\n- **MCP servers** (1): `trunk`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install trunk@claude-community` from `trunk-io/claude-code-plugin`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
